    <item>
      <title>The 2025 Reckoning: Data Wars, Power Grids, and the AI Job Abyss</title>
      <description>This 45-minute retrospective dissects the year AI became truly infrastructure—demanding massive energy, facing massive lawsuits, and fundamentally altering the global job market. We delve into the $22.5 billion SoftBank scramble, the landmark IP lawsuits defining ownership, and the chilling realization that junior coders are now functionally obsolete. We ask: Did the generative hype finally break the energy grid, and how exactly did Disney’s robot Olaf become the face of existential dread?</description>
